 {
  "kind": "text",
  "text": "The toggle is built and starts in the off state. I checked it in a contact sheet and a final frame at 1.2s, but I haven't played it through live.\n\n- **Layers:** `Track Off` (grey), `Track On` (green), `Knob` and `Check`.\n- **Timing:** the toggle starts at 0.4s and everything has settled by about 1.0s, inside your 1.2s target.\n- **Knob:** it slides from left to right, stretching wide mid-travel and then squashing tall on arrival. It overshoots by about 9px before settling.\n- **Track:** `Track On` fades in over the grey one between 0.4s and 0.8s, which gives the colour crossfade.\n- **Checkmark:** it draws itself in and fades up in green inside the knob, starting at 0.62s as the knob lands.\n\nI also set the background to a light grey (`#f2f2f7`) so the white knob stands out. The overshoot and squash amounts are easy to change if you want it snappier or softer.",
